# Review: StudioPlugin

The generation core is solid and tested. `generate.test.ts` covers the `generate` op end to end
against a mock provider: kind resolution, Connector credentials, variant append, cover seeding,
`NoGenerationService`, and async enqueue/resume. The storyboard operations and the Studio template
have their own tests. The type set, the default `image/*`, `video/*` and `audio/*` renderers,
gallery, lightbox and card surfaces, and the generator selector all exist, but the React side is
covered only by stories without play functions.

Two parts of the spec are not built, and one type has diverged:

- **The F-4 navigation hub is missing.** The app graph builder adds no "Studio" section and no
  virtual "Artifacts" node, and there is no `ArtifactsArticle`. Creating a MediaArtifact goes
  through plain `SpaceOperation.AddObject`, so nothing routes it under an Artifacts node.
- **Uploading a file as a Variant (F-2.3) and the `GenerateForm` override surface (F-1.3) are missing.**
  The upload control that exists fills a URL field of the generation request; it does not append a
  `Variant` with `content: Ref<File>`.
- **`MediaArtifact` has no `instructions`.** The prompt is a field of the persisted `request` record,
  which replaces `config`; `meta` is gone. `generate` reads the prompt from `config.prompt`, not
  `instructions.text`.

